#: ../../gm0/source/docs/common-mechanisms/power-transmission/power-transmission-glossary.rst:2
msgid "Power Transmission Glossary"
msgstr "Glosario de transmisión de potencia"

#: ../../gm0/source/docs/common-mechanisms/power-transmission/power-transmission-glossary.rst:18
msgid "C2C"
msgstr "C2C"

#: ../../gm0/source/docs/common-mechanisms/power-transmission/power-transmission-glossary.rst:20
msgid ""
"Center to center (C2C) refers to the distance between the centers of a pair "
"of :term:`sprockets <Sprocket>`, pulleys or :term:`gears <Gear>`. This will "
"affect :term:`chain <Chain>`/:term:`belt <Timing Belt>` tension and gear "
"meshing, so calculating this correctly is essential."
msgstr ""
"Centro a centro (C2C) se refiere a la distancia entre los centros de un par "
"de :term:`piñones <Sprocket>`, poleas o :term:`engranajes <Gear>`. Esto "
"afectará a la tensión de la :term:`cadena <Chain>`/:term:`correa "
"dentada<Timing Belt>` y al engrane de los engranajes, por lo que es esencial"
" calcularlo correctamente."

#: ../../gm0/source/docs/common-mechanisms/power-transmission/power-transmission-glossary.rst:15
msgid "Clearance Diameter"
msgstr "Diámetro libre"

#: ../../gm0/source/docs/common-mechanisms/power-transmission/power-transmission-glossary.rst:38
msgid "GT2 Belt"
msgstr "Cinturón GT2"

#: ../../gm0/source/docs/common-mechanisms/power-transmission/power-transmission-glossary.rst:35
msgid "HTD Belt"
msgstr "Correa HTD"

#: ../../gm0/source/docs/common-mechanisms/power-transmission/power-transmission-glossary.rst:37
msgid ""
"HTD belt is a type of synchronous timing belt commonly used on drivetrains. "
"It is available in different widths to accommodate different sized pulleys. "
"The most common is HTD3 (3mm :term:`Pitch`) and HTD5 (5mm :term:`Pitch`) "
"belts, as these are compatible with goBILDA :term:`COTS` pulleys. See "
":term:`Timing Belt`"
msgstr ""
"La correa HTD es un tipo de correa dentada síncrona que se utiliza "
"habitualmente en chasises. Está disponible en diferentes anchuras para "
"adaptarse a poleas de diferentes tamaños. Las más comunes son las correas "
"HTD3 (3mm :term:`Pitch`) y HTD5 (5mm :term:`Pitch`), ya que son compatibles "
"con las poleas goBILDA :term:`COTS`. Ver :term:`Correas dentadas"

#: ../../gm0/source/docs/common-mechanisms/power-transmission/power-transmission-glossary.rst:21
msgid "Idler"
msgstr "Rodillo"

#: ../../gm0/source/docs/common-mechanisms/power-transmission/power-transmission-glossary.rst:23
msgid ""
"An idler :term:`gear <Gear>`, :term:`sprocket <Sprocket>`, or pulley is one "
"that is purposely not used for driving anything else on the :term:`shaft "
"<Shaft>`. The purpose of this idler is, in the case of gears, to transfer "
"power to another direction."
msgstr ""
"Un rodillo :term:`engranaje <Gear>`, :term:`piñon <Sprocket>`, o polea es "
"aquella que no se utiliza a propósito para accionar nada más en el "
":term:`eje <Shaft>`. El propósito de esta polea es, en el caso de los "
"engranajes, transferir potencia a otra dirección."

#: ../../gm0/source/docs/common-mechanisms/power-transmission/power-transmission-glossary.rst:25
msgid ""
"For :term:`chain <Chain>` and :term:`belt <Timing Belt>`, idlers are more "
"common, and are usually adjustable to maintain tension."
msgstr ""
"Para :term:`cadena <Chain>` y :term:`correa <Timing Belt>`, los rodillos "
"tensores son más comunes, y suelen ser ajustables para mantener la tensión."

#: ../../gm0/source/docs/common-mechanisms/power-transmission/power-transmission-glossary.rst:12
msgid "Outside Diameter (OD)"
msgstr "Diámetro exterior (OD)"

#: ../../gm0/source/docs/common-mechanisms/power-transmission/power-transmission-glossary.rst:9
msgid "Pitch"
msgstr "Paso"

#: ../../gm0/source/docs/common-mechanisms/power-transmission/power-transmission-glossary.rst:6
msgid "Pitch Diameter (PD)"
msgstr "Diámetro exterior (OD)"

#: ../../gm0/source/docs/common-mechanisms/power-transmission/power-transmission-glossary.rst:26
msgid "Sprocket"
msgstr "Piñón"

#: ../../gm0/source/docs/common-mechanisms/power-transmission/power-transmission-glossary.rst:28
msgid ""
"A sprocket is a mechanical part that transfers power through its cogs, which"
" fit into chain. It is similar to a :term:`gear <Gear>`, except that instead"
" of meshing with another gear, the sprocket meshes with chain. See "
":term:`Chain`"
msgstr ""
"Un piñón es una pieza mecánica que transfiere potencia a través de sus "
"dientes, que encajan en la cadena. Es similar a un :term:`engranaje <Gear>`,"
" salvo que en lugar de engranar con otro engranaje, el piñón engrana con la "
"cadena. Véase :term:`Cadena"

